+ "corrections": [
+  {
+   "id": "C1",
+   "severity": "minor",
+   "claim_as_published": "PASS at K=4 AND at K=6 (queueing safe). Every request got its FULL 4096-token budget (stop=limit at gen==max_tokens = the intended n_predict budget, NOT pool exhaustion). No 500s, no deaths.",
+   "what_the_raw_rows_actually_say": "In the K=6 cell (fixprice.json candidates[0].cells[1]), requests 0-3 returned generated_tokens=4096 with stop_type='limit', but requests 4 and 5 returned 898 and 877 tokens with stop_type='eos' and truncated=false -- a NATURAL finish, not the budget. So 4 of 6 hit the budget and 2 of 6 stopped early on their own.",
+   "why_it_matters": "The two queued requests are exactly the ones that test what happens PAST the slot count. Because they finished naturally at ~900 tokens they never asked the pool for their full 4096, so the worst case at K>K_cap was NOT exercised by the evidence offered for the 'queueing safe' claim. The claim rested on rows that did not test it.",
+   "is_the_underlying_claim_true": "YES -- verified this session with the evidence the original claim lacked. See k6_forced_full_budget_recheck: K=6 against a fresh n_ctx=81920 server with ignore_eos forcing every request to its full 4096-token budget gave 6/6 HTTP 200, 6/6 at the full budget, 0 truncated, 0 errors, server healthy after. So the CLAIM holds and the published EVIDENCE did not support it -- two different statements, and only the second is the defect.",
+   "corrected_text": "PASS at K=4, and PASS at K=6 with the caveat that in the ORIGINAL K=6 cell only 4 of 6 requests reached the 4096-token budget (stop_type='limit'); the two QUEUED requests finished naturally at 898 and 877 tokens (stop_type='eos', truncated=false), so that cell did not exercise the worst case. A separate forced-full-budget run (ignore_eos) is the evidence that does.",
+   "rederived_from_raw_rows": {
+    "k6_cell_found": true,
+    "n_requests": 6,
+    "n_at_full_budget_stop_type_limit": 4,
+    "n_finished_naturally_stop_type_eos": 2,
+    "natural_finish_token_counts": [
+     898,
+     877
+    ],
+    "any_truncated": false,
+    "all_http_200": true
+   }
+  },
