+   "id": "C2",
+   "severity": "minor",
+   "claim_as_published": "our scored kernel requests machine_shape NvidiaL4 (scripts/kaggle/submission_kernel/kernel-metadata.json); the 96GB RTX PRO 6000 is a COMPETITOR's request; the only nvidia-smi read this project holds (results/kaggle_env_probe.json -> P100 16GB) is from a different kernel with no machine_shape",
+   "what_the_repository_record_actually_says": "ops/known-issues.md lines 2705-2712 record that Kaggle switched the ARC-AGI-3 competition's ACCELERATOR POOL from H100 to `g4-standard-48` on 2026-05-07, per Kaggle staff posts (threads 697720/697944), and that Google Cloud's machine-type docs identify g4-standard-48 as one NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Server Edition with 96GB GDDR7. A competitor's scored notebook running Gemma-4-31B on 'RTX Pro 6000' is cited there as CORROBORATION of the pool change, not as the source of the claim.",
+   "why_it_matters": "'A competitor's request' implies one entrant chose an unusual machine. The record describes a pool-level change affecting the competition. Getting this backwards understates how loose the scored VRAM envelope may actually be -- which is the exact question the parent lane was asked to establish rather than assume.",
+   "is_the_conservative_sizing_still_correct": "YES. exp5866's UNVERIFIED_EXTRAPOLATION status and its decision to size against the 16GB class are correct and well-supported, and the labelling is present in all three of the lane's artifacts. The only direct nvidia-smi read this project holds from any Kaggle kernel is a Tesla P100-PCIE-16GB (results/kaggle_env_probe.json, verified this session), from a kernel with no machine_shape. Whether the pool or the kernel's requested machine_shape governs a scored ARC run is unconfirmed.",
+   "corrected_text": "Kaggle moved the ARC-AGI-3 competition accelerator pool to g4-standard-48 (one RTX PRO 6000, 96GB) on 2026-05-07 per Kaggle staff posts; our submission kernel requests machine_shape NvidiaL4; whether the requested shape or the pool governs the scored run is UNCONFIRMED; the only direct read we hold is a 16GB P100 from a different kernel. Status remains UNVERIFIED_EXTRAPOLATION and the conservative 16GB-class sizing stands.",
